\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Teacher signal quality degrades with position} (100 MATH-500 problems, 1 trajectory each). (a) Reverse KL divergence KL$(p_s \| p_t)$ decays from 2.09 in the first 50 tokens to $\sim $0.24 by position 1000. Dashed line shows the token-level log-prob gap, which nearly coincides with the reverse KL. (b) Teacher entropy drops from 0.26 to 0.12 while teacher-student agreement rises from 79\% to 93\%. At later positions, the teacher is effectively rubber-stamping the student's choices.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:signal}{{1}{2}{\textbf {Teacher signal quality degrades with position} (100 MATH-500 problems, 1 trajectory each). (a) Reverse KL divergence KL$(p_s \| p_t)$ decays from 2.09 in the first 50 tokens to $\sim $0.24 by position 1000. Dashed line shows the token-level log-prob gap, which nearly coincides with the reverse KL. (b) Teacher entropy drops from 0.26 to 0.12 while teacher-student agreement rises from 79\% to 93\%. At later positions, the teacher is effectively rubber-stamping the student's choices}{figure.caption.1}{}}
